From 528bbb8e89df811804f15ee42639e655cd32f203 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jan Forst <ensonador@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 07:41:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] LOOM-8: domino. A fifth weave rule: the track's own hits are
 the triggers and the woven pattern's notes advance one step for each hit,
 each layer looping at its own length (a rest in the note layer is a silent
 hit). The note playhead is per-track runtime state, advanced once per fired
 trigger (not on hold/pulse cover or on ratchet hits), preserved by CONTINUE
 and reset by a new weave setup; KEEP AS PATTERN writes one trigger cycle at
 the trigger pattern's length. No format change: WV_DOMINO is appended to the
 rule enum. domino.xy; t_domino; the manual

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
